/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(* This sheet provides power input, decoupling, and I2C connection to the Raspberry Pi.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* Power is supplied via USB-C and externally accessible +5V net.) Tj
T* (  - Local filtering includes multiple decoupling capacitors across +5V and GND.) Tj
T* (  - Capacitor values include 10uF, 100nF, and 100uF types for a wide frequency response.) Tj
T* (  - All capacitors are referenced to a solid ground plane.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* The +3.3V I2C bus is connected to the Raspberry Pi header.) Tj
T* (  - Pull-up resistors \(3.3k) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(\) are provided on SDA and SCL lines.) Tj
T* (  - I2C lines connect to GPIO2 \(SDA\) and GPIO3 \(SCL\) on the Pi.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* Raspberry Pi 40-pin header is used.) Tj
T* (  - Only essential pins are shown connected \(power, I2C, GND\).) Tj
T* (  - Remaining pins are left unconnected for clarity.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* External +5V is routed through header H1 \(pin 1 = +5V, pin 2 = GND\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* All unused GPIO and power pins on the Pi header are shown unconnected \(crossed\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* Decoupling capacitor placement is designed to minimize voltage ripple on the +5V rail.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* GND is a shared plane for I2C, decoupling, and Pi ground connections.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* Series resistor placeholder. Populate with 0) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
