/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(* This schematic defines four analog output channels with flexible signal selection,) Tj
T* (  op-amp buffering, and ESD protection routed to a labeled patch panel.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* The MCP4728 DAC \(U601\) provides four independent analog voltage outputs \(CH1) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(CH4\).) Tj
T* (  - I2C-controlled; fixed address default is 0x60 \(EEPROM can be used to reassign\).) Tj
T* (  - Output range: 0 to 5V referenced to GND.) Tj
T* (  - Local bypass capacitor \(C601 = 100nF\) stabilizes the supply.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* The PCA9685 PWM controller \(U603\) supplies four PWM outputs and four select lines.) Tj
T* (  - I2C address set to 0x40.) Tj
T* (  - Channels LED0,2,4,6 provide PWM signals \(CHx-DOUT-PWM\).) Tj
T* (  - Channels LED1,3,5,7 control signal selection \(CHx-DOUT-SEL\).) Tj
T* (  - Duty cycles can be set to 0% or 100% for use as digital outputs.) Tj
T* (  - Decoupling capacitor \(C603 = 100nF\) placed at VDD.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* Each channel includes an SPDT analog switch \(U646) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(U649, SN74LVC1G3157DCKR\).) Tj
T* (  - B1 input receives CHx-DAC-OUT.) Tj
T* (  - B2 input receives CHx-DOUT-PWM.) Tj
T* (  - S input is driven by CHx-DOUT-SEL \(from PCA9685\).) Tj
T* (  - S = 0 selects DAC \(analog\), S = 1 selects PWM \(digital\).) Tj
T* (  - Local decoupling capacitors \(C610) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(C613, 100nF\) stabilize each switch.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* The selected signal is buffered by a precision op-amp \(U645) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(U648, OPA333\) configured for unity gain.) Tj
T* (  - Provides low-impedance drive suitable for analog or digital outputs.) Tj
T* (  - Series resistor \(49.9) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(\) on each output adds protection and improves signal integrity.) Tj
T* (  - H2 - H5 Provide an option to include the op amp or bypass it.) Tj
T* (    - Jumping 1-2 & 3-4 will include the op amp in the output circuit) Tj
T* (    - Jumping 1-3 will bypass the op amp entirely) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* Outputs are routed to a 4-pin patch panel connector \(CN111\).) Tj
T* (  - Each channel output is labeled CHx-PATCH-PANEL-OUT.) Tj
T* (  - Connector part: KF2EDGV-5.08-6P, labeled ) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<201c> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(Analog Out Patch Panel) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<201d> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* ESD protection is provided on each output using unidirectional TVS diodes \(D441) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(D444, PESD5V0S1UL\).) Tj
T* (  - Designed for ESD transient suppression to IEC 61000-4-2.) Tj
T* (  - Clamping behavior protects against brief high-voltage events.) Tj
T* (  - Diodes are placed near the connector to suppress external transients.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* Ground is shared across DAC, PWM, switching, and analog output stages.) Tj
T* (  Proper layout isolation is recommended to minimize cross-domain noise coupling.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* This design enables software-defined analog output routing:) Tj
T* (  - Use DAC for stable analog voltage output.) Tj
T* (  - Use PWM or static logic for digital control signals.) Tj
T* (  - Outputs are selectable per channel, with seamless runtime switching.) Tj
