/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(Drawing Notes ) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2014> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( Relay Driver Circuit) Tj
T* () Tj
T* <> Tj
T* () Tj
T* (MCP23008 GPIO Expander \(U120\)) Tj
T* <002a00200054006800650020004d0043005000320033003000300038002000700072006f00760069006400650073002000380020004700500049004f0020006c0069006e00650073002000760069006100200074006800650020004900b2004300200069006e0074006500720066006100630065002e> Tj
T* <002a0020004900b2004300200061006400640072006500730073002000690073002000730065007400200074006f00200030007800320030002000760069006100200061006400640072006500730073002000700069006e0073002000410032002c002000410031002c0020004100300020005c00280061006c006c002000740069006500640020004c004f0057005c0029002e> Tj
T* (* External 10k) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( pull-ups on SDA and SCL are required if not already provided elsewhere on the bus.) Tj
T* (* A 100nF decoupling capacitor \(C303\) is placed near VDD.) Tj
T* (* GPIOs default to Hi-Z input mode at power-up. Until firmware configures the pins as outputs, they are not actively driven.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Relay Driver and Inversion Behavior) Tj
T* (* GPIO outputs from the MCP23008 are connected to the ULN2803A Darlington array \(U122\), which drives eight 5V relay coils.) Tj
T* (* The ULN2803A is electrically inverting:) Tj
T* (    - Input HIGH ) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2192> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( Output LOW \(GND\)) Tj
T* (    - Input LOW ) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2192> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( Output floating \(open\)) Tj
T* (* In this configuration, the relay coils are connected between +5V and ULN outputs, so the circuit behaves logically non-inverting:) Tj
T* (    - MCP output HIGH ) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2192> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( Relay ON) Tj
T* (    - MCP output LOW ) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2192> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( Relay OFF) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Startup Behavior and Pull-Down Resistors) Tj
T* (* At startup, the MCP23008 GPIOs are not yet configured, and remain in Hi-Z state.) Tj
T* (* 100k) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( pull-down resistors \(R100) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(R108\) are placed on the inputs of the ULN2803A, ensuring that the ULN inputs are held LOW during this time.) Tj
T* (* This prevents unintended relay activation before firmware takes control and ensures relays are OFF at boot.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Firmware Programming Requirements) Tj
T* (* Firmware must:) Tj
T* (    1. Configure MCP23008 GPIOs as outputs: IODIR = 0x00) Tj
T* (    2. Optionally initialize output latch register: OLAT = 0x00 to start with all relays OFF) Tj
T* (    3. Use GPIO writes to control relays:) Tj
T* (        - Write 1 \(HIGH\) ) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2192> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( Relay ON) Tj
T* (        - Write 0 \(LOW\) ) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2192> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( Relay OFF) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Relay and LED Circuitry) Tj
T* (* Relay Type: SRD-05VDC-SL-C) Tj
T* (    - 5V coil) Tj
T* (    - SPDT contacts) Tj
T* (    - Coil resistance: ~70) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
T* /F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(* Each relay drives an indicator LED \(LED110) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(LED117\) in parallel with the coil, via a 1k) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( series resistor \(R110) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(R117\), illuminating when the relay is ON.) Tj
T* (* The ULN2803A includes internal flyback diodes, protecting against inductive spikes from the relay coils.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Terminal Blocks and Contact Isolation) Tj
T* (* Each relay) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2019> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(s output is routed to a 3-pin terminal block \(CN101) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(CN108\).) Tj
T* (* Relay contacts are electrically isolated from control and logic sections.) Tj
T* (* Contact naming follows the CPCx.y convention:) Tj
T* (    - Example: CPC1.3 = Relay 1 NC contact) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Power and Decoupling) Tj
T* (* Relay coils are powered from +5V via ULN2803A.) Tj
T* (* Local decoupling:) Tj
T* (    - C1 = 100nF ceramic) Tj
T* <0020002000200020002d00200043003100340020003d002000340037003000b5004600200065006c0065006300740072006f006c0079007400690063> Tj
T* (    - Both placed near U122 to ensure supply stability during relay switching) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Grounding and Power Plane Notes) Tj
T* (* Logic, relay drivers, and relay coils share a common GND.) Tj
T* <> Tj
T* (* If needed, use local copper fills or stitching vias to create a return path with low inductance near the ULN outputs.) Tj
