/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(* This sheet defines 8 isolated digital input channels, protected and level-shifted for monitoring via I2C.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* Input connector CN109 receives 8 external digital signals \(CIN401) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(CIN408\).) Tj
T* (  - Each input line is protected with a SMF33A TVS diode to ground.) Tj
T* (  - TVS clamps only above ~36V, suitable for 24V or higher industrial systems.) Tj
T* (  - Inputs are filtered and routed through individual level-shift circuits.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* Each input line \(CIN401) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(CIN408\) is processed by a discrete NPN transistor stage \(Q401) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(Q408\).) Tj
T* (  - Transistor type: MMBT3904) Tj
T* (  - Input resistor: 150k) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( \(limits input current\)) Tj
T* (  - Base divider: 150k) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( / 24k) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( to set logic threshold near 5V) Tj
T* (  - Pull-down resistor: 470k) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( ensures input goes low when unconnected) Tj
T* (  - Outputs \(DIN401) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(DIN408\) are open-collector logic-level signals) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* Processed outputs \(DIN401) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(DIN408\) feed into the MCP23008 GPIO expander \(U401\).) Tj
T* (  - MCP23008 address pins \(A0, A1, A2\) are configured via hard-wired levels to address 0x21) Tj
T* (  - I2C interface connects to SDA/SCL and is pulled up externally) Tj
T* (  - Decoupling capacitor \(C406 = 100nF\) is placed near VDD) Tj
T* (  - Internal RESET is pulled up via 10k) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( resistor \(R401\)) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* The MCP23008 digitizes the input states for I2C monitoring.) Tj
T* (  - Outputs are active-low, reflecting the collector state of each NPN stage) Tj
T* (  - 5V logic compatible, shared with host I2C bus) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* GND is the reference for all comparator stages and is assumed shared with the incoming signal ground.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* This circuit provides robust overvoltage protection, signal conditioning, and digital isolation for interfacing field-level signals with a microcontroller or embedded system via I2C.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (* Programming Notes:) Tj
T* (  - Each input pin \(DIN401) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(DIN408 ) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2192> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
( GP0) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<2013> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
(GP7\) should be configured as an **input**:) Tj
T* (      - `IODIR = 0xFF`) Tj
T* (  - Enable **internal weak pull-ups** \(typical 100k) Tj
/F3 25.411763280320827 Tf
<03a9> Tj
/F2 25.411763280320827 Tf
<002c0020007e00320035002000b5007300200072006900730065002000740069006d00650020007700690074006800200035003000700046005c0029003a> Tj
T* (      - `GPPU = 0xFF`) Tj
T* (  - Input logic is **active-low**:) Tj
T* (      - `0 = active/high input`, `1 = inactive/low input`) Tj
T* (      - Software should **invert logic** when interpreting input state) Tj
